sibility, adaptability.\n\nLet's assess each:\n\nA: strengths: anticipate dangerous situations (decision quality, safety), see complex connections (technical competence), excellent spatial vision (technical), very good leadership (crew cooperation). Concerns: not good at taking criticism (adaptability), unorganized (reliability/attention). No explicit stress resilience info.\n\nB: strengths: very conscientious (reliability), handles stress well (stress resilience), good at assessing weather (technical), excellent computer skills (technical). Concerns: grumpy, uncooperative (crew cooperation, communication). No explicit decision speed.\n\nC: strengths: makes correct decisions quickly (decision quality), 100% reliable (reliability), creates positive atmosphere (crew cooperation). Concerns: difficulty communicating ideas (communication), egocentric (crew cooperation), not willing to further education (adaptability). Technical competence not explicit.\n\nD: strengths: responds to unexpected events adequately (stress resilience), concentrates well (attention), solves problems extremely well (technical competence, decision), takes responsibility seriously (responsibility). Concerns: arrogant (crew cooperation), weak leadership (crew cooperation). No explicit reliability but maybe okay.\n\nWhich candidate overall best? Need balanced across criteria. C has reliability and decision quality, but communication issues and lack of adaptability. B has stress resilience and conscientiousness but uncooperative. D has problem solving, responsibility, concentration, but arrogance and weak leadership. A has anticipation, technical, leadership but unorganized and poor at criticism.\n\nProbably candidate D seems strong on technical, attention, responsibility, but concerns about arrogance and weak leadership may affect crew cooperation. However, crew cooperation is important. Candidate C has positive crew atmosphere despite egocentric? Actually creates positive atmosphere, but difficulty communicating ideas and egocentric may be issues. Reliability is perfect.\n\nCandidate B has stress resilience and conscientiousness but uncooperative.\n\nWe need to pick one. I think candidate C might be best because reliability 100%, correct decisions quickly, positive crew atmosphere, despite communication difficulty. But egocentric and not willing to further education could be concerns for long-term development. However, the role is safety-critical; reliability and decision quality are top. Crew cooperation is also important; positive atmosphere suggests good cooperation despite egocentric? Might be okay.\n\nCandidate D has strong problem solving and responsibility, but arrogance and weak leadership could be serious for crew.\n\nThus I might recommend Candidate C.\n\nWe need to state recommendation and give evidence.\n\nSince no prior discussion, we can just state.\n\nMETADATA_JSON vote: Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
