iability, decision quality, calm under crisis, technical competence, positive crew atmosphere. Concerns: communication difficulty, egocentric, limited education willingness.\n\nWe have new info: B handles stress very well; D responds adequately; A unknown stress resilience.\n\nWe need to incorporate this into our argument. Perhaps we can argue that B's strong stress resilience and conscientiousness make him a strong alternative, but his communication issues (pretentious, wrong tone) and lack of reliability data may be concerns. D has good problem solving and responsibility, but only adequate stress resilience and moody/loner concerns. A lacks stress data.\n\nThus we may still recommend C, but we need to discuss the new evidence and compare.\n\nWe should also maybe ask about reliability for B, D, A? But we can just argue.\n\nOur vote remains Candidate C.\n\nLet's craft a concise public message: agree with previous recommendation, note B's stress resilience but concerns about communication and lack of reliability; D's adequate stress but moody/loner; A unknown stress; thus C remains best.\n\nProceed."}
